`WrapConfig` and `wrap_many_with` keep a difference that already lies within the face band, on either side, instead of folding it onto the opposite face. The band is 256 units of roundoff, `128 ε`, times the perpendicular face width (`WrapConfig::face_slack`, `WrapConfig::face_tolerance`). The default `wrap_many` / `mi_wrap_many` path is the engine wrap, bit for bit. C passes `mi_wrap_config` to `mi_wrap_many_with` (`mi_wrap_face_slack`, `mi_wrap_face_tolerance`). C++ passes `minimage::WrapConfig` to `wrap_many`.
